From e13a6c0888d2baf99bae3991cbfa9bd9d850f970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:57:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(site): copy the act-report icon and the icon notice to
 the site

984b2af6c added assets/ui/act-report.png without its site copy, and the
#1696 and #1945 notice rows of assets/ui/LICENSES.md never reached
site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt. test_component_static_icons_and_license_match_app
requires both copies byte-identical.

Fixes #2801

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt   |  45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 site/static/icons/act-report.png | Bin 0 -> 567 bytes
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 site/static/icons/act-report.png

diff --git a/site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt b/site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt
index 9c776bbf3..0b46ecba6 100644
--- a/site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt
+++ b/site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ source-form distributions.
     OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE
     USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
 
-## Original artwork (assets/ui/svg/*.svg except heart.svg, and the PNG rasterised from each: the op-*, tool-*, tree-*, badge-* and act-* glyphs)
+## Original artwork (assets/ui/svg/*.svg except heart.svg and act-report.svg (the Tabler `banner` glyph, in the Tabler section below), and the PNG rasterised from each: the op-*, tool-*, tree-*, badge-* and act-* glyphs)
 
 These glyphs are our own drawings. Each has an SVG master in
 assets/ui/svg/, rasterised to its 32 px PNG by `cargo xtask icons`, drawn
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ and joins): the operation glyphs (`op-*`, #661 slice 1) from what each
 operation does - a cutter and its path; the tool kinds (`tool-*`, #661
 slice 2) from each cutter's silhouette; the browser's setup rows
 (`tree-*`), the operation status badges (`badge-*`) and the CamCraft
-actions (`act-*`). They replace the earlier original PNGs (post, sim,
+actions (`act-*`, except `act-report`: the Tabler `banner` glyph below). They replace the earlier original PNGs (post, sim,
 fixture, debug-info and the operation originals) and the Tabler glyphs
 that stood in for the stock, model, work offset, generate, frame-all and
 eye rows (box-model, cube, transform, player-play, maximize, eye,
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ subjects, our renderings; no license notice owed, and they are not part of
 the Tabler set below. (The exclusion lists here are the only record of
 which pixels are ours, so both headings name the same files.)
 
-## Tabler Icons (file-plus, folder-open, file-import, device-floppy, arrow-back-up, arrow-forward-up, trash, tools, heart PNGs and assets/ui/svg/heart.svg - loaded by crates/ui/src/egui_app/icons.rs)
+## Tabler Icons (file-plus, folder-open, file-import, device-floppy, arrow-back-up, arrow-forward-up, trash, tools, heart PNGs and assets/ui/svg/heart.svg, act-report PNG and assets/ui/svg/act-report.svg - loaded by crates/ui/src/egui_app/icons.rs)
 
 Outline glyphs from Tabler Icons (https://tabler-icons.io), version 3.49.0,
 MIT (below): recolored to white at load; shapes otherwise unmodified.
@@ -64,6 +64,11 @@ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tabler/tabler-icons/main/icons/outline/heart.s
 Its PNG is rasterised from that master. The existing MIT notice below
 also covers this icon.
 
+`assets/ui/svg/act-report.svg` and its PNG are Tabler's too: the `banner`
+glyph, used for the Report door (#1696). Its SVG master sits in
+assets/ui/svg/ beside our own drawings, but the glyph is Tabler's and its
+shape is unmodified.
+
 MIT License
 
 Copyright (c) 2020-2026 Paweł Kuna
@@ -130,6 +135,40 @@ MIT License (tracing)
 
 Copyright (c) 2019 Tokio Contributors
 
+## AI provider transport (crates/app/src/ai/http.rs, keychain.rs - #1945; native builds only)
+
+`reqwest` (HTTP client), `tokio` (request runtime), `hyper`, `hyper-util`
+and `http-body-util` (HTTP), with `rustls`, `rustls-webpki`, `rustls-pki-types`,
+`ring` and `untrusted` (TLS), `webpki-roots` (the Mozilla CA roots), and
+`keyring` with `keyring-core` and its per-OS stores
+(`apple-native-keyring-store` and `security-framework`,
+`windows-native-keyring-store`, `zbus-secret-service-keyring-store` and
+`secret-service` with the RustCrypto `aes`, `cbc`, `hkdf`, `hmac`, `sha2`,
+`subtle` and `zeroize` crates) are crates.io dependencies. Licences, as each
+crate declares them: MIT (tokio, hyper, hyper-util, http-body-util);
+MIT OR Apache-2.0 (reqwest, keyring, keyring-core and its
+stores, rustls-pki-types, security-framework, secret-service, the RustCrypto
+crates except subtle, zeroize); Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT (rustls); ISC
+(rustls-webpki, untrusted); Apache-2.0 AND ISC (ring); BSD-3-Clause
+(subtle); CDLA-Permissive-2.0 (webpki-roots: the root certificate data,
+from Mozilla's CA programme). Retained as a licence condition, same posture
